<mxCell id="n38" value="FINDING F1 (High). Zero-priest agyari: the booking is created at status=requested with NO BookingMobed and NO notification to anyone (services no longer notify admins). The behdin is told &#x27;request has been sent&#x27;. It can never be accepted — accept/decline requires a BookingMobed row. The request silently dies. Code comments admit it is &#x27;out of scope&#x27;, but it is a live false-confirmation." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="1310" width="320" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="e39" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#b85450;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.2;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n15" target="n38"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="n40" value="FINDING B2 (Med). Services picker and priest picker are dynamic WhatsApp Flows. Same simulator gap as B1 (unrenderable in /chat) AND the priest step only accepts &#x27;priest_&lt;id&gt;&#x27; text — no name synonyms — so a multi-priest booking is untestable by hand without internal user ids. Also needs Flow registration + keys (all empty in repo)." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="90" width="330" height="175" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="e41" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#d6b656;exitX=1;exitY=0.4;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.2;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n2" target="n40"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
</root>
